# Lesson 2, from the 1NT response exercise (hand c, adjusted so the play is simple): raise 1NT to game.
title: Raise 1NT to game
id: L02-29
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.4, 2.6
student: S
board: 29
dealer: N
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AK3    AQ2    Q862   J74
  E  4      JT987  J74    Q953
  S  T875   K654   AK5    86
  W  QJ962  3      T93    AKT2

auction:
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = 10+ points: game
     key: 10 HCP opposite 15-17 makes at least 25. Bid game.
     not 2NT: 2NT shows 8-9. Did you count 10?
     not Pass: Did you add it up? 10 plus 15-17 is at least 25.
     not *: With 10+ opposite 15-17, can you bid game directly?
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 1NT showed 15-17 points and a balanced hand. Your 10 points
  bring your side to at least 25, enough for game, so you bid 3NT. North
  is declarer, because she bid no-trump first, and so East will lead to
  the first trick.

play:
  1   E HJ  S H4  W H3  N HQ
  2   N D2  E D4  S DA  W D3
      note: Declarer's plan: there are nine top tricks, so take them. Start with diamonds, playing dummy's high cards first.
  3   S DK  W D9  N D6  E D7
      note: The ♦K.
  4   S D5  W DT  N DQ  E DJ
      note: Back to declarer's ♦Q.
  5   N D8  E C3  S C6  W S2
      note: Declarer's last diamond is a winner.
  6   N HA  E H8  S H5  W C2
      note: Now the hearts.
  7   N H2  E H9  S HK  W CT
      note: A heart to dummy's ♥K.
  8   S S5  W S6  N SA  E S4
      note: Back to declarer's spades.
  9   N SK  E HT  S S7  W S9
      note: The ninth trick.
  10  N C4  E C5  S C8  W CK
      note: Nine tricks are in. Declarer gives up the rest.
  11  W CA  N C7  E C9  S ST
  12  W SQ  N S3  E CQ  S S8
  13  W SJ  N CJ  E H7  S H6
      note: 9 tricks: 3NT made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: take the nine top tricks: two spades, three hearts and
  four diamonds.

  3NT made. Your 10 points were all partner needed to hear to know your
  side had enough for game.
